# Firmware too large for the initramfs, which write_to_drive.sh fetches
# (tools/fetch-firmware.sh firmware/storage.list) and copies onto the
# storage partition, where the kernel looks too (/storage/lib/firmware).
# Same format as stock.list, plus `link <name> <target>` lines for
# linux-firmware's symlinks (FAT32 has none): the fetch writes them to
# lib/firmware/.links and the kernel's firmware loader follows them.
#   lf = linux-firmware 20260916
# NVIDIA GSP-RM 570.144 for nouveau (M39): Turing, Ampere, Ada and
# Blackwell GB20x (RTX 5070 = GB205). Too large for the initramfs (the GSP
# images are 30-63 MB), so write_to_drive.sh puts them on the storage
# partition (/storage/lib/firmware). `link` lines are linux-firmware's
# symlinks, which FAT32 cannot hold: the kernel's firmware loader follows
# them from lib/firmware/.links.
